SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2023: Pakistan","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2023/country-chapters/pakistan","claim":"Throughout 2022, the government continued to control media and curtail dissent; authorities harassed and at times detained journalists and other civil society members for criticizing officials and policies.","locator":"lines 68-76","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Year-end human-rights synthesis with direct coverage of 2022 conduct and concrete examples.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective annual summary covering 2022 under Sharif.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the Sharif-led government, though individual arrests were usually carried out by police or regulators rather than the PM personally.","contrary_evidence":["Some cases were framed as law-enforcement or sedition enforcement, so this is evidence of suppression rather than proof of direct PM orders in each case."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.8","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Report 2023: Pakistan","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://www.hrw.org/world-report/2023/country-chapters/pakistan","claim":"Women, religious minorities, and transgender people continued to face violence, discrimination, and persecution, while authorities failed to provide adequate protection or hold perpetrators to account.","locator":"lines 69-71, 83-95, 115","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Year-end human-rights synthesis with multiple specific examples across vulnerable groups.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers 2022 conditions under Sharif.","ruler_attribution":"This describes state protection failures under Sharif's government, but much of the violence was perpetrated by non-state actors or inherited institutions.","contrary_evidence":["The report does not show a single Sharif-directed campaign against these groups; it shows a failure to protect and remedy."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.7","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/pakistan/freedom-world/2023","claim":"Pakistan's military exerts enormous influence, intimidates the media, and enjoys impunity for indiscriminate or extralegal use of force.","locator":"overview section, lines 84-86","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Established democracy/rights monitor with a concise country overview and year-end synthesis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective synthesis of 2022 conditions.","ruler_attribution":"This is partly inherited structural context, but it also constrains and shapes what the Sharif government could or did do about security-force abuse and media pressure.","contrary_evidence":["The statement is structural and not a direct account of a specific Sharif instruction or event."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.8","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistani journalist Imran Riaz Khan arrested","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-07-07","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/07/pakistani-journalist-imran-riaz-khan-arrested/","claim":"Police arrested journalist Imran Riaz Khan multiple times; CPJ called the repeated arrests pure harassment and said authorities should let journalists safely criticize state institutions, including the military.","locator":"lines 516-520","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct press-freedom advocacy with contemporaneous details and named victim reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"The article explicitly ties the case to the government led by Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, though the arrest was carried out by police on complaint/cases.","contrary_evidence":["The legal cases were presented as criminal complaints, so this is evidence of retaliatory enforcement rather than a court finding of unlawful intent."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistani journalists Jameel Farooqui and Ilyas Samoo arrested; Farooqui remains in detention","publisher":"Committee to Protect Journalists","publication_date":"2022-08-23","url":"https://cpj.org/2022/08/pakistani-journalists-jameel-farooqui-and-ilyas-samoo-arrested-farooqui-remains-in-detention/","claim":"Police arrested journalists Jameel Farooqui and Ilyas Samoo, and CPJ said authorities should stop harassing them in retaliation for their work and release them immediately.","locator":"lines 516-521","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous alert with named actors, arrest dates, and direct attribution to police action.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to the Sharif-led domestic environment, but the arrests were made by provincial police, not the PM personally.","contrary_evidence":["The case file references public-order or criminal allegations, so the evidence is about retaliation risk and abuse of process rather than a final legal judgment."],"lenses":["3B.2","3B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Braving the Storm: Enforced disappearances and the right to protest in Pakistan","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-08-11","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/asa33/5872/2022/en/","claim":"Peaceful protests by families of the disappeared were met with intimidation, harassment, arbitrary detention, and violence by state actors, including unnecessary force against protesters in Karachi.","locator":"briefing summary and the Karachi protest account","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Detailed rights briefing with specific protest incidents and first-hand accounts.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in-period and directly about 2022 protest handling.","ruler_attribution":"This reflects state conduct under Sharif's government, but the abuse appears to have been carried out by police and intelligence agents rather than ordered in a public PM statement.","contrary_evidence":["The protests concerned enforced disappearances inherited from prior years, so the state failure is partly long-running rather than newly created in 2022."],"lenses":["3B.1","3B.2","3B.4","3B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan: Authorities must respect and facilitate people’s right to protest","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-06-28","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/06/pakistan-authorities-must-respect-and-facilitate-peoples-right-to-protest/","claim":"Amnesty said authorities used unnecessary or excessive force to disperse Lyari protesters over power shortages, describing baton-charging and tear-gassing of people exercising their right to protest.","locator":"quoted response paragraphs and background section","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous rights statement tied to a specific protest and police response.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This was police conduct under the Sharif government, but not a PM-only action and not proof of a centrally ordered repression policy by itself.","contrary_evidence":["Police said the protests blocked traffic, so the case involves a public-order dispute as well as a rights violation allegation."],"lenses":["3B.5","3B.8","3B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ex-Pakistani PM Khan supporters hold nationwide protests, demand political change","publisher":"Euronews / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-11-05","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/11/05/pakistan-politics-khan","claim":"After Imran Khan was shot, his supporters staged nationwide protests that sometimes clashed with security forces, and police used tear gas to disperse protesters blocking roads.","locator":"lines 610-624","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong independent contemporaneous coverage of a major domestic-security episode.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This shows the domestic unrest and force response during Sharif's tenure, but it does not establish a PM-specific order to use force.","contrary_evidence":["The same report also says protesters blocked roads and some clashed with security forces, so the episode is not one-sided."],"lenses":["3B.8","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Pakistan 2022 Floods Response Plan","publisher":"United Nations in Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://pakistan.un.org/en/197498-pakistan-2022-floods-response-plan","claim":"The Government of Pakistan and the UN jointly launched the 2022 Floods Response Plan after severe monsoon weather had declared 72 districts calamity hit.","locator":"lines 56-56 and surrounding summary","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN humanitarian coordination page with direct, dated response-plan details.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and directly tied to the government response under Sharif.","ruler_attribution":"This is government-led disaster response under Sharif, though the floods themselves were inherited/climate-driven and not a ruler-caused event.","contrary_evidence":["The source measures response planning and scale of disaster, not the full effectiveness of implementation on the ground."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"وزیراعظم نے سیلاب سے متاثرہ افراد کی امداد کیلئے ریلیف فنڈ قائم کر دیا","publisher":"Radio Pakistan Urdu","publication_date":"2022-08-06","url":"https://urdu.radio.gov.pk/06-08-2022/ozir-aaathm-n-silab-s-mtathr-afrad-ki-amdad-kile-rilif-fn-kaem-kr-dia","claim":"Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif established a relief fund for flood victims, appealed for donations, and said the government had released 5 billion rupees immediately for flood relief.","locator":"lead paragraph / first report paragraph","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official state broadcaster in Urdu, with a concrete PM announcement and a specific relief amount.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sharif's public disaster-response direction.","contrary_evidence":["This is an announcement of relief, not proof that relief reached all intended recipients or that it was sufficient."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"PM directs to provide cash assistance worth Rs50,000 per family to flood-affectees","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-08-15","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/15-08-2022/pm-shehbaz-orders-payment-of-cash-assistance-to-flood-affected-people-within-three-days","claim":"Shehbaz Sharif directed that Rs50,000 per flood-affected family be provided within three days and asked for transparent transfer through BISP supervision.","locator":"lead paragraph / report summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official broadcaster report of a dated PM instruction with a concrete amount and timing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct PM instruction, so this is strong ruler attribution for crisis response.","contrary_evidence":["The report is official and does not independently verify delivery quality or targeting accuracy."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt starts immediate cash distribution among flood affectees in country: PM","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-08-19","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/19-08-2022/govt-starts-immediate-cash-distribution-among-flood-affectees-in-country-pm","claim":"The government began immediate cash distribution of Rs25,000 per affected family, and Sharif said relevant institutions were working daily with international partners to provide relief.","locator":"lead paragraph / report summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official report with concrete cash-distribution details and direct PM remarks.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Direct government response under Sharif, though still self-reported by state media.","contrary_evidence":["The report reflects the start of disbursement, not full coverage or a final evaluation of adequacy."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Govt launches '4R Framework' for Pakistan Floods 2022","publisher":"Radio Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-12-21","url":"https://www.radio.gov.pk/21-12-2022/pm-shehbaz-launches-4rf-for-pakistan-floods-2022","claim":"Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif launched the Resilient Recovery Rehabilitation and Reconstruction Framework for the 2022 floods.","locator":"lead paragraph / report summary","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official broadcaster report of a specific PM-launched recovery framework.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022, near year-end.","ruler_attribution":"Direct PM-led recovery planning, though it remains a framework announcement rather than completed implementation.","contrary_evidence":["A framework launch is not the same as measurable recovery success."],"lenses":["3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Flood-Affected Women in Pakistan Need Urgent Help","publisher":"Human Rights Watch","publication_date":"2022-09-02","url":"https://www.hrw.org/news/2022/09/02/flood-affected-women-pakistan-need-urgent-help","claim":"Among the flood-affected were at least 650,000 pregnant women and girls, many of whom lacked access to the healthcare facilities and support needed for safe delivery.","locator":"lines 610-618","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Independent rights analysis with concrete humanitarian figures and explicit protection concerns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This is not Sharif-caused harm, but it is a direct test of the government's protection and relief response to a major domestic crisis.","contrary_evidence":["The article focuses on urgent need, not on whether government relief ultimately reached everyone adequately."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UN Women puts women and girls at the heart of flood response in Pakistan","publisher":"United Nations in Pakistan","publication_date":"2022-09-07","url":"https://pakistan.un.org/en/198187-un-women-puts-women-and-girls-heart-flood-response-pakistan","claim":"UN Women reported relief distributions, cash grants, women-friendly spaces, and gender-based-violence response services for flood-affected women and girls in Pakistan.","locator":"main article text on relief items and service scale-up","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN program update with concrete service and relief actions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly in 2022 and directly relevant to flood response.","ruler_attribution":"This is government-and-UN-coordinated crisis response under Sharif, though execution involved UN partners rather than the PM alone.","contrary_evidence":["The page shows active response, but not whether all protection needs were met."],"lenses":["3B.7","3B.9","3B.10"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I reviewed roughly 25-40 documents across HRW, Freedom House, Amnesty, CPJ, UN/OCHA/UN Women, Radio Pakistan, Euronews/Reuters, Dawn, and some blocked State Department excerpts.
- I kept sources that did one of three things: show Sharif-era repression, show concrete domestic-crisis protection, or establish authority/attribution.
- I rejected repeated syndications of the same Reuters stories when they did not add new facts.
- I rejected out-of-period material from 2021 and later 2023-2024 pages unless they clearly summarized 2022 conduct.
- I rejected broad economic or general governance pages that did not connect to physical safety, protest treatment, or vulnerability protection.
- The State Department custom excerpt pages were technically blocked/forbidden in this environment, so I did not rely on them.
- I did not use the client matrix.

**Remaining gaps**
- There is still no direct public record of Shehbaz Sharif personally ordering police or intelligence operations in the protest/media cases.
- I did not find a clean public record of a 2022 Sharif-led reform that improved oversight, complaint handling, or accountability for abuse.
- The strongest negative evidence is about protest and media suppression, not a national campaign of mass terror; the record looks like recurring repression and selective coercion rather than systematic state terror.
- The strongest positive evidence is flood relief and reconstruction planning; more search would help only if there are PMO, interior ministry, cabinet, or parliamentary records tying specific restraint or abuse-prevention decisions directly to Sharif.
